# Local Chaos and cloud cleanup — 2026-09-06

The reviewed local cleanup starts from `25d5081b`. All 95 removed files were
untracked; no tracked Unreal assets or source files were deleted. The local
`MCPGameProject.Build.cs` dependency additions were restored to the existing
main version. This commit records the cleanup rather than publishing the
discarded experiments.

## Chaos

- Removed 48 untracked files: four legacy native pillar/review source files,
  26 old Blueprint/map/geometry assets, and 18 legacy authoring, review, or
  one-time tuning scripts.
- Preserved all tracked assets, including `BP_ChaosPillar_BP_V02`, its FX
  manager, projectile/review Blueprints, `NS_ChaosPillarFX_BP_V02`, and
  `L_ChaosPillarBPReview_V02`.
- Preserved the three local manual-authoring scripts referenced by
  [the current QA record](ChaosPillar_BP_V02_TwoStage_QA.md):
  `enable_chaos_pillar_bp_v02_manual_ue.py`,
  `finalize_chaos_pillar_manual_trigger_ue.py`, and
  `setup_chaos_pillar_bp_v02_manual_map_ue.py`. They remain untracked and are
  not a newly published or idempotent authoring workflow.

## Clouds

- Removed 47 untracked files: 30 disconnected historical comparison images
  and 17 historical review, analysis, or import scripts.
- Preserved 149 files in the reviewed cloud scope, including source textures,
  manifests, QA evidence, generation dependencies, and material refinements.
- V018 remains the saved baseline. V019 remains a visual-review candidate;
  its recorded preview did not replace the persistent map binding.
- Old version numbers and `tune_` prefixes alone do not establish that a file
  is disposable. V019 depends on V018 and older generation helpers, so those
  dependencies were retained.

## Review and verification

- Independent reviews approved both exact removal lists and their hashes.
- Byte scans of 2,894 project assets found no tracked-asset references to the
  26 removed asset candidates. Independent UTF-8/UTF-16 scans found no
  remaining code, configuration, or asset references to the Chaos removal set.
- In an isolated UE 5.6 editor without the legacy native source or assets,
  the current BP review map loaded. Its 106-package project dependency closure
  contained no removal candidates or `/Script/MCPGameProject` or
  `/Script/UnrealMCP` dependency. The four retained Blueprints use engine
  Actor/CameraActor parents and compiled with zero errors and warnings.
- After cleanup, all 95 removal paths were absent, all 152 explicitly retained
  local files were present, and the project Source tree matched main.
  The project C++ gate passed without an approval-code override.
- The cleaned local `MCPGameProjectEditor Win64 Development` target built
  successfully with UE 5.6. The project module and corrected UnrealMCP module
  were rebuilt.
- This cleanup does not assert new PIE visual approval or cook/package coverage.
  Existing visual limitations in the QA record remain applicable.

## Recovery

Before removal, all 95 files and the prior local `Build.cs` were archived and
verified by per-file SHA-256. The local deliverables are
`cleanup-recovery-2026-09-06.zip` and `cleanup-manifest.json` in this task's
outputs. The manifest lists every removed path, hash, and retained file.
The archive is local recovery material and is not committed to Git. The
[tracked manifest](Analysis/LocalCleanup/20260906_manifest.json) retains the
exact reviewed path inventory and hashes without machine-specific paths.

Unrelated `Content/Template/Empty.umap`, attachments, the nested Sites
repository, and unfinished cloud work remain outside this cleanup.
